# Old pre-reorganization directories at the repository ROOT only.
# The leading slash is load-bearing: unanchored `entity/` and `utils/` match at
# ANY depth, so they silently swallowed src/entity/ and src/utils/. Existing
# files survived only because git honours already-tracked paths over .gitignore,
# but any NEW file added there would have vanished without a warning — and
# `git mv src src/aicds` would have recreated the problem one level deeper.
/entity/
/utils/
/Dataset/
BioSentVec_PubMed_MIMICIII-bigram_d700.bin

# System design visualization (local-only, detailed architecture diagrams)
.system-design-visualization

# The GroupKFold-on-SUBJECT_ID replacement splits (aicds.config.CORRECTED).
# These are MIMIC-III derived and fall under the PhysioNet DUA, so they are
# generated locally and never committed. Anchored, per the note above.
#
# The pre-commit hook does NOT cover this path: its rule is
# `^data/(raw|folds)/`, which requires a literal '/' after "folds" and so does
# not match "folds_grouped/"; and its 20-distinct-HADM_ID fallback greps for a
# literal `HADM_ID[=: ]*\d{6}` token, which fold files (`123456_symptom,...`)
# do not contain. This .gitignore entry is the only thing standing between
# `git add -A` and a DUA violation.
/data/folds_grouped/

# Results kept locally, not committed -- same rule as results/ above.
# Regenerate on a Linux box with the 21 GB BioSentVec model; see docs/findings/11.
results_corrected/
